'' --emit-doc over a type with a 'derive' line (RFC 0019): the line is in the type's header, not a
'' field named derive; what it gives the type is listed as members the compiler wrote ('=' '<>',
'' '<' '>' '<=' '>=', ToText); and 'derive as int32' stays a field.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.edocd/cache
'' CLEAN: build/.edocd
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 --emit-doc build/.edocd/out tests/modules/src/docmod/derivedoc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: ### Cell\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: A point on a grid.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: derive equal, order, hash, text
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: declare function ToText( ) as ustring
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: operator <= ( byref a as Cell, byref b as Cell ) as boolean
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: Written by the compiler: 'derive order'.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: | `as int32 row` | the row, from 0 |
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: `derive as int32`
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edocd/out/main.derivedoc.md :: | `derive equal
